If $\mathrm{T}$ be $(\mathrm{h}, \mathrm{k})$ then as in $\mathrm{Q} .44$
\tan \alpha=\frac{2|\sin \alpha|}{\sqrt{\mathrm{h}^{2}+\mathrm{k}^{2}+4 \mathrm{~h}-6 \mathrm{k}+9 \sin ^{2} \alpha+13 \cos ^{2} \alpha}}

\begin{array}{l}
\Rightarrow h^{2}+k^{2}+4 h-6 k+9 \sin ^{2} \alpha \\
+13 \cos ^{2} \alpha=4 \cos ^{2} \alpha \\
\Rightarrow \mathrm{h}^{2}+\mathrm{k}^{2}+4 \mathrm{~h}-6 \mathrm{k}+9=0
\end{array}

$\therefore$ Locus of $T$ is $x^{2}+y^{2}+4 x-6 y+9=0$

The centre of the required circle lies at the intersection of $2 x-3 y-5=0$ and $3 x-4 y-7=0 .$ Thus, the coordinates of the centre are $(1,-1)$.
Let $r$ be the radius of the circle.

\begin{array}{l}
\pi r^{2}=154 \\
\Rightarrow \frac{22}{7} r^{2}=154 \Rightarrow r=7
\end{array}

Hence, the equation of required circle is

\begin{array}{l}
(x-1)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=7^{2} \\
\Rightarrow x^{2}+y^{2}-2 x+2 y-47=0
\end{array}

